WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.483
Every tenant in Orchard Core has its own settings and its own configuration.

00:00:05.483 --> 00:00:09.693
In this video, we'll see where they are stored, how the layers combine,

00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:13.411
how to prepare a tenant before it exists, and how to keep them

00:00:13.411 --> 00:00:15.160
in a database or in Azure.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.734
Each tenant runs as a shell.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:25.740
A shell has settings, such as its state and its URL prefix, and

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.850
a configuration, which the modules of the tenant read through IShellConfiguration.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.789
By default, both are files in the App_Data folder.

00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:37.864
The settings of all tenants are in tenants.json.

00:00:37.864 --> 00:00:42.591
The configuration of each tenant is in its own appsettings.json, in the Sites

00:00:42.591 --> 00:00:45.040
folder, under the name of the tenant.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.868
Orchard Core finds the tenants in two places:

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:54.360
the entries of tenants.json, and the sections of the configuration that have a State.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.370
The ORCHARD_APP_DATA environment variable moves the App_Data folder.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.919
The path can be relative to the application or absolute, and Orchard Core

00:01:03.919 --> 00:01:06.970
tries to create the folder if it doesn't exist.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:15.991
The configuration of a tenant is built in layers, and the last layer wins.

00:01:15.991 --> 00:01:18.763
The first layer is the host application:

00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:24.970
appsettings.json, user secrets in development, environment variables, and command line arguments.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.342
Next come the files in App_Data that apply to every tenant:

00:01:29.342 --> 00:01:32.240
appsettings.json, and one for the environment.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.980
Environment variables and command line arguments are applied again after them, so they still win.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:44.715
Then comes the section named for the tenant, under OrchardCore, taken from any of those sources.

00:01:44.715 --> 00:01:48.470
Its values override the shared ones, for that tenant only.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.837
Last is the file of the tenant itself.

00:01:51.837 --> 00:01:56.773
It has no OrchardCore section and no variant for the environment, and Orchard

00:01:56.773 --> 00:02:00.520
Core writes to it, for example when the tenant is set up.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.814
To prepare a tenant before it exists, add a section named for it

00:02:08.814 --> 00:02:12.030
under OrchardCore, with a State of Uninitialized.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.182
Orchard Core treats any section that has a State as a tenant, and

00:02:16.182 --> 00:02:19.340
uses its other values when the tenant is set up.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.063
With the Tenants feature enabled in the Default tenant, the Tenants page under

00:02:26.063 --> 00:02:28.813
Multi-Tenancy lists the prepared tenant.

00:02:28.813 --> 00:02:35.510
Acme is Uninitialized, with its category and database provider from the configuration, and a Setup button.

00:02:35.962 --> 00:02:37.249
Let's open Edit.

00:02:37.249 --> 00:02:39.062
It shows the same values:

00:02:39.062 --> 00:02:44.385
the Url Prefix and the Description, and under Database Presets, the database provider

00:02:44.385 --> 00:02:46.782
that the setup of this tenant uses.

00:02:50.982 --> 00:02:55.438
To change the configuration of a tenant that exists, use a section named

00:02:55.438 --> 00:02:57.151
for it, without a State.

00:02:57.151 --> 00:03:01.606
Here, the Default tenant gets a smaller maximum file size for media, and

00:03:01.606 --> 00:03:04.062
every other tenant keeps the default.

00:03:04.812 --> 00:03:10.123
Environment variables use the same layout, with a double underscore between levels.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:14.776
The first applies to every tenant, the second to the Default tenant, and

00:03:14.776 --> 00:03:17.222
the third to the tenant named Acme.

00:03:17.972 --> 00:03:23.355
Don't give a tenant the name of a configuration section, such as Media or Email.

00:03:23.355 --> 00:03:28.362
Tenant sections and module sections share the same path under OrchardCore.

00:03:32.562 --> 00:03:38.292
To give every tenant the same database, set DatabaseProvider and ConnectionString once, at

00:03:38.292 --> 00:03:40.799
the root of the OrchardCore section.

00:03:40.799 --> 00:03:45.692
The Default tenant gets a table prefix of its own, so its tables stay apart.

00:03:46.442 --> 00:03:52.728
RequireTablePrefix demands a table prefix when a tenant is created, for providers that support one.

00:03:52.728 --> 00:03:57.757
TablePrefixPattern generates it from a Fluid template, such as the name of the

00:03:57.757 --> 00:04:01.408
tenant, and SchemaPattern does the same for the schema.

00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:03.862
Both must be valid SQL identifiers.

00:04:04.612 --> 00:04:08.924
Tenants don't copy these shared values into their own files, so moving the

00:04:08.924 --> 00:04:12.912
application to another environment means changing them in one place.

00:04:17.112 --> 00:04:22.168
A module reads the configuration of its tenant by taking IShellConfiguration in the

00:04:22.168 --> 00:04:24.384
constructor of its Startup class.

00:04:24.384 --> 00:04:27.792
It binds a section to an options class with Configure.

00:04:28.542 --> 00:04:34.011
Name the section without an OrchardCore_ prefix, and group related settings by nesting,

00:04:34.011 --> 00:04:36.421
such as MyService, then MyProvider.

00:04:36.421 --> 00:04:39.772
The names of environment variables then stay short.

00:04:40.522 --> 00:04:43.962
In the host, ConfigureServices runs for each tenant.

00:04:43.962 --> 00:04:48.766
This code reads the UseCdn value of the Resources section from the tenant's

00:04:48.766 --> 00:04:51.791
configuration and sets it with PostConfigure.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.807
It changes the options only:

00:04:53.807 --> 00:04:57.662
the admin still shows the value saved in the site settings.

00:05:01.862 --> 00:05:04.399
The files in App_Data suit most sites.

00:05:04.399 --> 00:05:09.644
When several stateless hosts must create tenants and change their settings while they

00:05:09.644 --> 00:05:12.064
run, they can share a store instead.

00:05:12.064 --> 00:05:15.522
Orchard Core offers Azure Blob Storage and a database.

00:05:16.272 --> 00:05:23.319
For Azure, add the OrchardCore.Shells.Azure package, and call AddAzureShellsConfiguration on the Orchard Core

00:05:23.319 --> 00:05:24.912
builder of the host.

00:05:25.662 --> 00:05:28.550
Configure it under OrchardCore, Shells, Azure:

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:33.104
the connection string of the storage account, the name of the container, and

00:05:33.104 --> 00:05:34.714
optionally a base path.

00:05:34.714 --> 00:05:37.712
The container must exist before the host starts.

00:05:38.462 --> 00:05:43.250
The container holds tenants.json at its root, and a Sites folder with a

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:46.546
folder and an appsettings.json for each tenant.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:52.142
An appsettings.json at the root, and one for the environment, apply to every tenant.

00:05:52.892 --> 00:06:01.963
For a database, call AddDatabaseShellsConfiguration, and set DatabaseProvider and ConnectionString under OrchardCore, Shells, Database.

00:06:01.963 --> 00:06:07.752
The settings of the tenants go in one document, and their configurations in another.

00:06:08.502 --> 00:06:13.818
Both providers read their own options from the host configuration, not from the store.

00:06:13.818 --> 00:06:19.422
MigrateFromFiles copies the existing files of App_Data into a store that doesn't have them.

00:06:20.172 --> 00:06:23.955
The providers are meant for hosts that share tenants while they run, not

00:06:23.955 --> 00:06:27.203
for sharing configuration between development and production.

00:06:27.203 --> 00:06:31.712
To skip a provider in development, call it only when the environment isn't Development.

00:06:33.712 --> 00:06:36.526
That's how Orchard Core configures a tenant:

00:06:36.526 --> 00:06:41.873
its settings in tenants.json, its configuration in layers, presets for tenants that don't

00:06:41.873 --> 00:06:44.799
exist, and a shared store for stateless hosts.

00:06:44.799 --> 00:06:46.262
Thanks for watching.

